uw-ttyp0

UW ttyp0 is a family of monospaced bitmap screen fonts for X11 and the
Linux console. It includes regular, bold, and italic variants, Unicode
support, box drawing, Powerline symbols, Braille, and many international
scripts.

This package installs:

  * PCF fonts in /usr/share/fonts/X11/misc
  * OTB fonts in /usr/share/fonts/misc/uw-ttyp0
  * Linux console fonts in /usr/share/kbd/consolefonts
  * bdfmangle and its manual page
  * complete project documentation in /usr/doc/uw-ttyp0-2.1

After installation, refresh the font caches if necessary:

  fc-cache -f
  xset fp rehash

The Linux console fonts can be loaded temporarily with setfont. The
available sizes, encodings, and stylistic variants are selected by the
TARGETS_*.dat and VARIANTS.dat files in the source archive.
